# This file was written when the OpenShift strategy used `oc start-build --from-dir`.
# That approach was abandoned because:
#   1. Build pods are evicted due to ephemeral-storage limits on cluster nodes.
#   2. `--build-arg` is silently ignored by the S2I binary source strategy.
#
# The current `cargo build-image --target openshift` strategy builds the image
# locally with Docker/Podman and pushes only the final runtime image to the
# OpenShift internal registry — `oc start-build` is no longer invoked.
#
# This file is kept as a safety net in case `oc start-build` is re-introduced
# in the future. Without it, the Cargo build cache (>18 GB) would be uploaded.

target/
